rows=[(539, 'winter-put-away', 'Winter put away', 'The spring welcome starts by noticing shawls, blankets and sweaters retreating from use. This ordinary seasonal change can suggest the whole poem without a collage of blossoms, birds, Holi colour and divine figures.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 soft graphite and watercolor domestic crop. Inside an ordinary open wooden cupboard, a loosely folded muted grey wool shawl rests over one plain cream knit sweater on the lower-left shelf. Fabric has natural compression, one sleeve corner partly hidden and an uneven fold, not a retail stack. A softly lit strip of bare shelf and pale wall extends across the right half, with a little warmer daylight reaching the wool from outside the frame. Perspective, shelf support and cloth contact plausible. No mothballs, floral decorations, hangers, printed labels, people, elaborate furniture, clutter, signs of neglect, visible spring landscape or Holi props. Selective pencil at the fold and soft dilute grey/ochre wash; a quiet feeling of winter having passed. Opaque ivory paper, nothing glossy or symmetrical for display.'), (544, 'a-hawk-above-the-road', 'A hawk above the road', 'The poem notices hawks waiting on lamp posts during an ordinary journey. Focus on one of those birds and its practical perch, without inventing the exact location, a wildlife spectacle or a montage of prey and ducks.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 ink wash with muted gouache, viewed upward from a roadside. A single brown hawk rests naturally on the rounded top of an ordinary grey streetlamp head at the upper-left third. The lamp curves from a simple pole cropped at left. Both gripping feet supported, folded wings along the body, compact alert head turned slightly away, subtly hooked beak and tail extending behind; no eagle caricature or giant eye. Bird feathers are grouped in a few broad overlapping values, with selective detail at eye, beak and talon contact rather than every feather sharp. A very faint distant lamp post low on the right establishes everyday human surroundings; otherwise open grey-blue overcast sky. No prey, blood, five cloned birds, dramatic wingspread, military symbols, mystical aura, readable text or recognizable location. Quiet watchfulness and patient observation, a literary interpretation rather than a claimed photograph of the author’s sighting.'), (545, 'the-water-keeps-going', 'The water keeps going', 'The speaker compares persistence to a waterfall and the effort of a rocky ascent. A close fragment of water negotiating one ledge suggests continuing movement without a heroic summit panorama or an invented climber.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 matte gouache and restrained charcoal, close oblique view of a modest natural waterfall dropping over a dark irregular rock ledge. Show one cropped section of falling water rather than a whole towering waterfall: left-centre water thins across the stone lip, breaks into a few uneven translucent ribbons, and meets a partly cropped pool at the lower edge. Damp rock transitions naturally into drier muted grey-brown surface on the right. A small cluster of ordinary grasses rooted in a crevice leans away near the upper-left edge, no ornamental flowers. Leave the right third quieter as a broad rock plane with only selective edge marks. Plausible gravity, flow, contact spray and rock planes; no impossibly suspended water, giant droplets, repeated lace patterns or polished spa scene. Soft cloud light, muted mineral blue-grey and earth, strong but not theatrical movement. No climber, birds, rainbow, fantasy jungle, text or tourist landmark claim.')]
items=[]
